-- title:
--   Node total over a supersingular place via the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with $k$ algebraically closed and $q \nmid N$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (Y^q - X)(Y - X^q) \bmod q$, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha, h\beta$ for the two degeneracy embeddings of level $N$ into level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ over these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ for $P$. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ lying in `ssPlaces q N k` (so $w$ is rational, affine in the sense that both generators $j$, $j_N$ are $w$-integral, and its $j$-value lies in the supersingular set), and $c$ a pair of node coordinates $x, y$ in the ring $B := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ of elements of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ integral for both prolongations $R_1, R_2$ and for every place $V$ of the level-$Nq$ function field with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$, whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated over the coefficients of $K$ by $j$ and $j_{Nq}$; here $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\, w\, x = 0$, $\mathrm{ord}_{\varphi w}(\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\, w\, x) = 1$ with $\varphi = \mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N$ acting on places, and symmetrically for $y$. Let $\varpi \in A \cap K$. Assume $B$ is local and Noetherian with maximal ideal generated by the constant $\varpi$ together with $x$ and $y$; that for every $g \in B$ some constant $o$ makes $g - o$ a non-unit; the value-integrality law for $R$ at $w$, i.e. every $w$-node-integral $f$ has $V$-value in $A$ for all $V$ above $w$; and that $R$ satisfies `OrderLawFixed`. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\pi$ an irreducible element, $E \ge 1$, and $\iota$ a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $B$ onto the crossing model $\mathcal R = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ with $\iota(\varpi) = \mathrm{const}\ \pi$ and $\iota(x) = U \cdot \alpha_U$ for a unit $\alpha_U$. Let $f \in B$ have both residues $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1 w f$ and $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2 w f$ nonzero, with $\mathrm{ord}_w$ of the first and $\mathrm{ord}_{\varphi w}$ of the second nonnegative, and assume the two reading clauses: for $g \in B$ and $n \in \mathbb N$, if the first residue is nonzero of $w$-order $n$ then $\iota(g) - \gamma V^n \in (\mathrm{const}\ \pi, U)$ for some unit $\gamma$, and dually with $U^n$, $(\mathrm{const}\ \pi, V)$ and $\mathrm{ord}_{\varphi w}$ of the second residue. Finally let $T_{\mathrm{tot}}$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting exactly of those $V$ with $\mathrm{ord}_V f \ne 0$ and $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$. The conclusion is the equality in $\mathbb N_\infty$ of $\sum_{V \in T_{\mathrm{tot}}} (\mathrm{ord}_V f)^+$ with the finite sum, over the primes $Q$ of $\mathcal R$ with $Q \ne 0$ and $\mathrm{const}\ \pi \notin Q$, of $\mathrm{rank}_W(\mathcal R/Q)$ times the length, over the localisation of $\mathcal R$ at $Q$, of the localisation at $Q$ of $\mathcal R/(\iota(f))$.
--
--   This is the local comparison, at a supersingular node of the modular curve of level $Nq$ in characteristic $q$, between the total order of a function $f$ at the places of the level-$Nq$ function field reducing to $w$ and the total horizontal intersection multiplicity of the divisor of $\iota(f)$ on the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$; the orders of the two residues of $f$ at $w$ and at its Frobenius translate supply the two end slopes of the Gauss polygon. It feeds the counting and slope-drop statements at supersingular nodes, among them [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.card_eq_finsum_finrank_quotient_of_forall_iff_evalAt_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.card_eq_finsum_finrank_quotient_of_forall_iff_evalAt_eq_zero) and the two `exists_slopeDrop_eq_sum_div_depth_of_…` results.
